# Jira key on code changes

A meaningful code change names the WEL issue it belongs to. Look up an open issue that already covers the work before creating one. Put the key in the commit message: `WEL-85: Short reason`.

## Do the work anyway

- One issue covers the whole change. Do not open a new issue for each file, test, or follow-up edit.
- Typo fixes, formatting, generated files, lockfiles, and image-updater tag writes do not need an issue.
- If Jira cannot be reached, or the matching issue is unclear, make the code change and say which issue you would have used.
- Do not refuse a commit, push, or local edit because a key is missing.

## Capability index

If the change alters what a capability does, update `docs/current/capability-index.md` in that same change and run `python3 scripts/check-capability-index.py`. The procedure is in `.cursor/rules/agent-context.mdc`.

## Creating an issue

Create one only when nothing open covers the work. Use the existing epic. Stories and tasks can be created directly. Creating or moving an epic still waits for explicit approval.
